There are a number of ways to do that...

 1, Extreme AC so nothing hurts you
 2. Moderately good AC and regeneration
 3. Moderately good AC, high HP, low failure
     rates on healing spells, and the Eye
 4. Moderately good AC *or* high HP,
     combined with high damage
 5. Moderately good AC *or* high HP,
     combined with lots of good wands
 6. Moderately good AC *or* high HP,
     combined with high-level attack spells
     at low failure rates and the Eye
 7. Decent AC and HP, plus conflict
 8. Controlled teleport (ONLY works on
     levels that allow teleport)
 9. Some combination of the above

That's just the methods I know about.
Ideally you'll want to have more than one
of them at your disposal.  My personal
favorite combination is ridiculously low
AC plus obscenely high HP plus a ring
of regeneration plus controlled teleport
plus either high melee damage or
good rates on attack spells.  All of that
at once may be overkill, but can you
ever really have too much overkill?

Note that the Eye is not in general required
for spellcasting, but if you're going to rely
heavily on spells for survival in the face of
large summon storms, in the absence of
alternative ways to survive, it becomes
important. Since it also provides slotless
MR, it's a great wish for neutral non-wizards,
even if you don't need the power regeneration.

